"PulseFiles Help Shortcuts" = "Keyboard shortcuts:\n\n• Tab — Switch panes\n• Return or F4 — Open the selection, or rename/confirm text with Return while editing\n• F3 — Open the read-only text/hex viewer\n• F5 or F6 — Copy or move the selection to the opposite pane\n• F7 or Shift-F7 — Create a folder or file\n• F8 or Shift-Delete — Move the selection to Trash\n• Space — Preview with Quick Look\n• Backspace or Command-Up — Go to the parent folder\n• Command-[ or Command-] — Go back or forward\n• Command-Shift-G — Go to Folder\n• Command-N or Command-Shift-N — New folder or file\n• Command-C/X/V — Copy, cut, or paste with the clipboard\n• Command-Shift-. — Show or hide hidden files\n• Control-Command-1…7 — Sort by name, extension, kind, size, modified, created, or added date\n• Command-` — Toggle the Beta Terminal after enabling it in Settings\n• Command-Period — Cancel the active file operation\n\nOpen Settings to control the Beta Terminal and file-operation confirmations. Use folder pickers to grant PulseFiles access when macOS requires permission.";
"PulseFiles Help Shortcuts Debug" = "Keyboard shortcuts:\n\n• Tab — Switch panes\n• Return or F4 — Open the selection, or rename/confirm text with Return while editing\n• F3 — Open the read-only text/hex viewer\n• F5 or F6 — Copy or move the selection to the opposite pane\n• F7 or Shift-F7 — Create a folder or file\n• F8 or Shift-Delete — Move the selection to Trash\n• Space — Preview with Quick Look\n• Backspace or Command-Up — Go to the parent folder\n• Command-[ or Command-] — Go back or forward\n• Command-Shift-G — Go to Folder\n• Command-N or Command-Shift-N — New folder or file\n• Command-C/X/V — Copy, cut, or paste with the clipboard\n• Command-Shift-. — Show or hide hidden files\n• Control-Command-1…7 — Sort by name, extension, kind, size, modified, created, or added date\n• Command-` — Toggle the Beta Terminal after enabling it in Settings\n• Command-Period — Cancel the active file operation\n\nOpen Settings to control the Beta Terminal, file-operation confirmations, and Debug-only sandbox safeguards.";
